                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "While modern games increasingly copy each other, rely on AI-generated ideas, and cost $50 or more without offering anything new, HUE was a real hidden gem.\n\nMy library is already full of games like that, most of which end up refunded or collecting dust because of how boring they are. Finding HUE was a refreshing surprise. For just $1, you get the atmosphere of classic 2D games, unique mechanics I personally hadn’t encountered before, a simple story, and plenty of fun, clever puzzles.\n\nI’d almost forgotten that you don’t have to spend a fortune to enjoy a genuinely good game without constantly thinking, “I’ve seen this before.”\n\nHUE is fun, varied, and absolutely worth recommending for a relaxing evening. It’s especially perfect after finishing a great story-driven game that makes it hard to move on to something new. HUE doesn’t demand much from your brain; it simply lets you relax and enjoy some genuinely interesting gameplay.",
